<h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Microbiology Nonculture</h4>

<div class="etl-guide-columns">
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <!-- Step 1 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Create Non-culture Mappings</h5>
      <p class="text-sm mb-3">Before transforming your non-culture data, prepare the mapping files:</p>
      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
          <p><strong class="text-blue-300">a. Fluid Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">fluid_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">fluid_category</code></p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/microbiology_nonculture/clif_microbiology_nonculture_fluid_category.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_microbiology_nonculture_fluid_category.csv</a>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
          <p><strong class="text-blue-300">b. Method Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">method_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">method_category</code></p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/microbiology_nonculture/clif_microbiology_nonculture_method_category.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_microbiology_nonculture_method_category.csv</a>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
          <p><strong class="text-blue-300">c. Organism Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">micro_order_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">organism_category</code></p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/microbiology_nonculture/clif_microbiology_nonculture_organism_category.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_microbiology_nonculture_organism_category.csv</a>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
          <p><strong class="text-blue-300">d. Organism Group:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">organism_category</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">organism_group</code></p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/microbiology_nonculture/clif_microbiology_nonculture_organism_groups.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_microbiology_nonculture_organism_groups.csv</a>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
          <p><strong class="text-blue-300">e. Result Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_category</code></p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/microbiology_nonculture/clif_microbiology_nonculture_result_category.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_microbiology_nonculture_result_category.csv</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-300 mt-2">The organism is read from the <em>order</em> name (<code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">micro_order_name</code>, e.g. "csf hsv pcr" → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">herpes_simplex_virus</code>), not from the result text. <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_category</code> is the standardized outcome (e.g. <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">detected</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">not_detected</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">indeterminate</code>).</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
      <p class="text-sm">Filter your non-culture data to include only inpatient hospitalizations.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 3 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Which <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_dttm</code> rows to keep</h5>
      <div class="bg-amber-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-amber-400/30 text-sm">
        <p class="mb-2">EHRs often emit several interim result rows for one order. CLIF 3.0 collapses the interim rows for negative results only:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-xs">
          <li>• <strong>Positive</strong> results — keep <strong>every</strong> interim / processing-step row as the EHR records it (interim and final values).</li>
          <li>• <strong>Negative</strong> results — keep only the <strong>final</strong> negative-result row, one row per order.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-300 mt-2">See <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/issues/180" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="underline text-blue-300 hover:text-blue-200">Issue #180</a> for the decision thread.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 4 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Final Cleanup</h5>
      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-xs">
          <li>• <strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">order_dttm</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">collect_dttm</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_dttm</code> timezone-aware in UTC</li>
          <li>• <strong>Reference range &amp; unit:</strong> carry <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">reference_low</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">reference_high</code> (numeric) and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_unit</code> as the source reports them</li>
          <li>• <strong>LOINC:</strong> populate <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_loinc_code</code> when the source has it (optional)</li>
          <li>• <strong>Raw names:</strong> keep <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">fluid_name</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">method_name</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">micro_order_name</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_name</code> exactly as the EHR reports them</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Quality Checks -->
    <div class="bg-green-500/20 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-400/30">
      <h5 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-green-300">Data Quality Checks</h5>
      <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
        <li>• Negative orders have exactly one row</li>
        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_category</code> is a value from the mCIDE result list</li>
        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">organism_group</code> matches the group listed for its <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">organism_category</code> in the mCIDE</li>
        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">collect_dttm</code> ≥ <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">order_dttm</code> and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">result_dttm</code> ≥ <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">collect_dttm</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
